  "body": "Part of #658. Filed on the maintainer's word (question dialog, 2026-11-12: \"File them as P2\"); useful whatever is decided about SolidCraft's UI (#655), because egui moves on either way.\n\nA throwaway trial, nothing merges: on a scratch branch bump egui / egui-winit / egui-wgpu / eframe / egui_kittest from =0.36.2 to 0.37 (Rust 1.95 is needed; ours says 1.90) with `egui_dock` taken from its open upstream PR for 0.37 or patched locally, and record what happens. The estimate on #658 (comment of 2026-11-12) lists what is expected: about 30 mechanical source lines in about 20 files, the `default_fonts` change, and egui_kittest 0.37 failing input widgets that have no accessible name.\n\nDone means: a comment on #658 with the compile errors by kind, the red tests by cause (counts), whether the viewport's own wgpu passes still build, and the result of `web/build-app-wasm.sh`; the scratch branch is deleted; the size estimate on #658 is corrected from the findings. No PR.",
